<title>NETHERLANDS: HOOGOVENS SHARES DIP AFTER INITIAL RISE.</title>
<headline>HOOGOVENS SHARES DIP AFTER INITIAL RISE.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch steel and aluminium group Hoogovens NV on Wednesday turned around to stand some six guilders down at 130.00 guilders after posting strong first half results.</p>
<p>The group reported a 40 percent leap in first half net profits, sparking an initial jump in the share price. But the move was short-lived and the shares slid from the high of 142.30 guilders.</p>
<p>Analysts and dealers said a 13 million guilder extraordinary charge meant the net profits were not as positive as initially thought.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
